From 17be0f00b685b318cf18953f8679878acf70b098 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:38:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Haas G82 and G89 post each hole's own dwell P

The Haas cycle signature was g|Z|R|Q for G82 and G89, so a second hole
with a different dwell in an open cycle group posted as a bare X Y block
and ran the first hole's modal P. The dwell now joins the signature for
G82, G83 and G89 (as #1820 did for G83 alone): a changed dwell closes the
group and re-issues the cycle with its own P. G89 always writes P, P0 for
a zero dwell, so a reopened G89 never inherits the old modal P.

Pinned by crates/post/tests/haas_dwell_cycles.rs.

Fixes #2350

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
